from above under Shukhov's glass roofs; the front garden behind its railing (the museum's own building page). Turned 135 degrees so the portico faces north-west to Volkhonka, as the ground file shows. Guessed: the building's dimensions (about 90 by 64 m), the pediment (drawn low and full width over the colonnade), the roof layout. No photographs were available. Refined 30 Sep 2026 (no photographs reachable; the ground file's OpenStreetMap outlines): the whole place moved 20 m east and 12 m south onto the building's outline, whose two holes match the glass-roofed Greek and Italian courtyards under the model's skylights."}